Below is a **PowerPoint-ready visual structure** you can paste into slides to show **what AWS Config managed rules and Azure Policy definitions have in common, and how they differ**. AWS Config managed rules are predefined, customizable checks that evaluate whether AWS resources comply with common best practices, while Azure Policy definitions are the JSON-described rules that Azure Policy evaluates against resources to determine compliance.[5][3]

